@page "/docs/components/bar"

<Seo Canonical="/docs/components/bar" Title="Blazorise Bar component" Description="Build responsive headers and sidebars with the Blazorise Bar component. Explore its structure, dropdowns, and application navigation examples." />

<DocsPageTitle Path="Components/Bar">
    Blazorise Bar component
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    Keep application navigation and common actions within easy reach.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Use the <Code>Bar</Code> component to help users move between the main areas of your application.
    It works as a horizontal header or a vertical sidebar, bringing navigation, branding, and actions such as search or account access into a consistent location.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Structure
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A typical <Code>Bar</Code> combines branding, a toggler, and a menu. Within <Code>BarMenu</Code>, <Code>BarStart</Code> and <Code>BarEnd</Code> group <Code>BarItem</Code> components that contain links, dropdowns, or other controls.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsAnatomy Label="Bar component anatomy" Caption="BarItem can contain a link, dropdown, or another control. The item structure shown in BarStart also applies to BarEnd.">
    <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="Bar" Description="The navigation container.">
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarBrand" Description="Branding at the start of a horizontal bar or top of a vertical bar." />
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarToggler" Description="Controls menu expansion or vertical bar collapse." />
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarMenu" Description="Contains navigation groups; collapses at the configured breakpoint in horizontal mode.">
            <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarStart" Description="Start menu in horizontal mode; sticky top menu in vertical mode.">
                <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarItem" Description="One menu item containing a link, dropdown, or another control.">
                    <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarLink" Description="A navigation link or action.">
                        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarIcon" Description="An icon for the item; required in compact vertical modes." />
                    </DocsAnatomyRegion>
                    <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarDropdown" Description="An alternative to a link; shown as a popout in BarMode.VerticalPopout.">
                        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarDropdownToggle" Description="The dropdown trigger.">
                            <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarIcon" Description="An icon for the trigger; required in compact vertical modes." />
                        </DocsAnatomyRegion>
                        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarDropdownMenu" Description="The dropdown's contents.">
                            <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarDropdownItem" Description="A link or action within the dropdown." />
                            <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarDropdownDivider" Description="An optional separator between groups of items." />
                            <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarDropdown" Description="An optional nested dropdown that repeats this structure." />
                        </DocsAnatomyRegion>
                    </DocsAnatomyRegion>
                </DocsAnatomyRegion>
            </DocsAnatomyRegion>
            <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarEnd" Description="End menu in horizontal mode; sticky bottom menu in vertical mode.">
                <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="BarItem" Description="Uses the same item structure as BarStart." />
            </DocsAnatomyRegion>
        </DocsAnatomyRegion>
    </DocsAnatomyRegion>
</DocsAnatomy>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Examples
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Application Header" ElementId="bar-top-bar">
        A typical horizontal Bar has a brand, primary navigation, utility actions, and an account dropdown.
        Use <Code>BarStart</Code> for main navigation and <Code>BarEnd</Code> for actions that should stay aligned to the opposite side.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="TopBarExample" Outlined FullWidth FrameUrl="docs/components/bar/top-bar-iframe">
        <TopBarExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Horizontal Bar Theming">
        Match your navigation to your application’s look and feel in both light and dark layouts.
        Custom hover and selected colors help users recognize interactive items and see where they are.
        This example shows both color schemes with active and disabled items, plus a dropdown menu.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="HorizontalBarThemeExample" Outlined FullWidth
                            FrameUrl="docs/components/bar/horizontal-theme-iframe"
                            FrameHeight="400" FrameTitle="Horizontal Bar theme examples" />
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Navigation Target">
        <Code>BarDropdownToggle</Code> supports <Code>To</Code> the same way as other Blazorise link components.
        With the default <Code>Trigger="BarDropdownToggleTrigger.Auto"</Code>, setting <Code>To</Code> makes the label navigate while the chevron icon toggles the submenu.
        This example uses <Code>Match="Match.Prefix"</Code> so the parent link stays active while the example items navigate to sections of the Bar docs page.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="BarDropdownToggleToExample" Outlined>
        <BarDropdownToggleToExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Icon Trigger">
        This is the explicit form of the default <Code>To</Code> behavior.
        Use it when you want the intent to be visible in markup or when composing trigger flags elsewhere in the menu.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="BarDropdownToggleIconClickExample" Outlined>
        <BarDropdownToggleIconClickExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Route Matching">
        When users should be able to expand from either the label or icon, combine triggers with a flags expression.
        In this example, <Code>Trigger="BarDropdownToggleTrigger.ClickAny | BarDropdownToggleTrigger.RouteMatch"</Code> keeps the dropdown expanded whenever the current URL matches <Code>To</Code>.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="BarDropdownToggleRouteMatchExample" Outlined>
        <BarDropdownToggleRouteMatchExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Application Sidebar" ElementId="bar-vertical-sidebar">
        For a sidebar layout, place the vertical <Code>Bar</Code> inside <Code>LayoutSiderContent</Code>.
        This pattern keeps navigation, content, and header regions in predictable layout slots.

        Please see the <Anchor To="docs/components/layout">Layout docs </Anchor> for more information on setup with Sidebar.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="VerticalBarSideBarExample" Outlined FullWidth FrameUrl="docs/components/bar/sidebar-iframe">
        <VerticalBarSideBarExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<Alert Color="Color.Info" Visible>
    <AlertDescription>
        <Strong>Note:</Strong> The <Code>BarIcon</Code> is required for each <Code>BarLink</Code> or <Code>BarDropdownToggle</Code> when using <Code>BarMode.VerticalSmall</Code> or <Code>BarCollapseMode.Small</Code>, in order for it work correctly.
        For a full demo of the vertical bar in action, please check out the <Anchor To="https://demos.blazorise.com/wasm/bootstrap5/" Target="Target.Blank">Blazorise Bootstrap 5 demo</Anchor>.
    </AlertDescription>
</Alert>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Right-aligned Sidebar">
        You can create a right-aligned <Code>Vertical</Code> style <Code>Bar</Code> by following two key principles.
        <UnorderedList>
            <UnorderedListItem>
                Use <Code>Layout</Code> to place the <Code>LayoutSider</Code> after the main <Code>Layout</Code> section.
            </UnorderedListItem>
            <UnorderedListItem>
                Add <Code>RightAligned</Code> to dropdowns that should open toward the left side of the right rail.
            </UnorderedListItem>
        </UnorderedList>
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="VerticalBarRightAlignedExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <VerticalBarRightAlignedExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Vertical Bar Toggler">
        The <Code>BarToggler</Code> for a vertical Bar supports two modes:
        <UnorderedList>
            <UnorderedListItem><Code>BarTogglerMode.Normal (default)</Code></UnorderedListItem>
            <UnorderedListItem><Code>BarTogglerMode.Popout</Code></UnorderedListItem>
        </UnorderedList>
        These modes, along with an external implementation, provide three common implementations.
        <Paragraph>
            <Strong>1. Inline</Strong>
        </Paragraph>
        Add the <Code>BarToggler</Code> inside the vertical <Code>Bar</Code> to let the user collapse and expand the rail in place.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="VerticalBarInlineExample" Outlined>
        <VerticalBarInlineExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader>
        <Strong>2. Popout</Strong>

        Set <Code>Mode="BarTogglerMode.Popout"</Code> when the toggler should sit outside the collapsed rail.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="VerticalBarPopoutExample" Outlined>
        <VerticalBarPopoutExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader>
        <Strong>3. External (controlled by Top Bar)</Strong>

        In layouts with both a top bar and a sidebar, a top-bar toggler can control the sidebar by setting the <Code>Bar</Code> property.
        The example below uses two togglers inside the top bar.
        <UnorderedList>
            <UnorderedListItem>
                One controls the vertical Bar.
            </UnorderedListItem>
            <UnorderedListItem>
                One controls the horizontal Bar menu.
            </UnorderedListItem>
        </UnorderedList>
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="VerticalBarExternalExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <VerticalBarExternalExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Nested Dropdowns" ElementId="bar-nested-dropdowns">
        To create nested dropdowns, place a <Code>BarDropdown</Code> inside an existing <Code>BarDropdownMenu</Code>.
        This is useful for admin, reporting, and settings menus where the top-level item groups related actions.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="VerticalBarNestedDropdownsExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <VerticalBarNestedDropdownsExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Header on top">
        For an example where the horizontal <Code>Bar</Code> is “on top” of the vertical <Code>Bar</Code>, please look at <Anchor To="docs/components/layout" Target="Target.Blank">this example </Anchor> in the <Code>Layout</Code> docs.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Best Practices
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Keep Navigation Predictable
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Keep primary navigation stable across pages and order destinations by importance or user workflow. Use clear text labels, and provide an accessible label or tooltip when an item is represented by an icon alone. Dropdown hierarchies should remain shallow enough to scan and navigate comfortably.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Responsive Design
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Verify both collapsed and expanded states at every supported breakpoint. The toggler must remain easy to find, the active destination should be clear, and the focus order should stay logical whether the bar is horizontal or vertical.
</DocsPageParagraph>

